{"shortDescription":"Nasdaq futures slid more than 1% on Thursday as high-growth stocks faced renewed pressure after earnings from Tesla and Meta Platforms did little to allay concerns over AI spending, while a rebound in oil prices further dampened sentiment.The weakness follows a strong session on Wednesday when the…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Nasdaq futures slid more than 1% on Thursday as high-growth stocks faced renewed pressure after earnings from Tesla and Meta Platforms did little to allay concerns over AI spending, while a rebound in oil prices further dampened sentiment."]},{"type":"p","children":["The weakness follows a strong session on Wednesday when the tech-heavy Nasdaq led Wall Street higher as robust results from SpaceX ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:SPCX","text":"NASDAQ:SPCX"}}," and Super Micro ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:SMCI","text":"NASDAQ:SMCI"}}," rekindled optimism around AI-linked stocks."]},{"type":"p","children":["SpaceX dropped 2.3% and Super Micro fell 4.7% in premarket trading on Thursday as investors shifted their focus from earnings to the mounting cost of the AI buildout."]},{"type":"p","children":["Tesla ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:TSLA","text":"NASDAQ:TSLA"}}," fell 5.3% after the electric-vehicle maker cut its annual capital expenditure forecast, raising questions about the pace of its AI and robotics expansion."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meta's ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:META","text":"NASDAQ:META"}}," shares slipped 1.9% after the social media giant introduced new non-voting shares to help fund its costly AI push, reviving investor scrutiny of the substantial capital required to stay competitive in the race."]},{"type":"p","children":["The 'Magnificent 7' stocks were also down, with Amazon.com ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:AMZN","text":"NASDAQ:AMZN"}}," declining 1.6% and Nvidia ",{"type":"symbol","pa